-- Layer: library: shared mathematics over the core (the four layers: see the language-implementation-remainder node of task-graph/hyperactivity.cub).
-- lib/library/intlin.cub — the search side of linear arithmetic over Int (PLAN.md revision 7.9, 6 Nov 2026, git 2ca8d747aaa5:PLAN.md, §18.13 “F31–F32 — Reflection and certificates”, its part F32). The
-- verified checker (lib/library/intproof.cub: int-cert-check with int-cert-sound) translates an
-- integer claim to a word claim over doubled variables; the search for its multipliers is the
-- same translation followed by lib/bootstrap/lin.cub's directed Fourier–Motzkin search (omega-cert) or its
-- enumeration (find-cert) over the untyped codes of the fragment. Nothing here is trusted: what
-- the search produces goes through int-cert-check, whose soundness is the theorem. Loaded after
-- lib/library/intproof.cub; untyped, as lib/bootstrap/lin.cub is.
--
-- a typed word code read as a code of the fragment (addition is cwop #2)
lc-to-code : LinCode → Code
lc-to-code (lc-lit n) = cwlit n
lc-to-code (lc-var v) = cvar v
lc-to-code (lc-add a b) = cwop #2 (lc-to-code a) (lc-to-code b)
lc-to-code (lc-suc a) = cwsucc (lc-to-code a)
hyps-to-lst : Hyps → Lst (Code × Code)
hyps-to-lst hnil = lnil
hyps-to-lst (hcons l r rest) = lcons (lc-to-code l , lc-to-code r) (hyps-to-lst rest)
lst-to-mults : Lst Word → Mults
lst-to-mults lnil = munil
lst-to-mults (lcons c r) = mucons c (lst-to-mults r)
-- the searches over integer claims (hypotheses hs : IHyps, goal a ≤ b) are lib/bootstrap/lin.cub's omega-cert
-- and find-cert, helpers of the bootstrap files, untyped, so no checked definition calls them; a
-- reading does: #show int-cert-of (omega-cert (hyps-to-lst (int-hyps hs)) (lc-to-code (igoal-l a b))
-- (lc-to-code (igoal-r a b))). The search's result as the checker's multipliers (an empty list where
-- the search refutes):
int-cert-of : Opt (Lst Word) → Mults
int-cert-of (some l) = lst-to-mults l
int-cert-of none = munil
